+For single-worker user-space fixed costs, use `scripts/profile_http_instructions.py --binary /absolute/path/rgnix --work-dir /native/linux/new-directory` with Valgrind, OpenSSL and `/usr/sbin/nginx` installed on Linux. Add `--candidate /absolute/path/candidate` for a comparison, `--case proxy-16k` for larger responses (default `proxy-1k`), and `--extra-headers 64` for header-width sensitivity. Add `--nginx /usr/sbin/nginx` for the matched NGINX control and `--rotating-headers` to alternate those extra names on every request, exercising cache fallback. Each sample subtracts a matching startup/warmup/shutdown run from a run with 2,000 extra exact-payload validated responses, using Cachegrind's flat instruction counts. Three rounds retain six samples per binary; require every A/A pair and the group CV to stay within 1%. Signed function deltas and failed controls are preserved. This measures neither kernel work nor shared-cache contention, and cannot establish throughput, P99 or multi-worker capacity. Keep the optional wakeup probe disabled during these runs.

