 The [further instruction reduction](validation-hyper-instructions2-2026-10-24.md) compares local `5cf9ef5` with `57b069e`. Constructing transport URIs only on connection misses and borrowing paths without percent escapes lowers matched instructions by another 2.34% for 1 KiB, 2.32% for 16 KiB and 1.07% with 64 extra headers, with passing 1% A/A and CV checks. A deferred h2c watch-clone trial increased copies and instructions and was withdrawn. The final candidate passes 434 Hyper runtime checks plus 105 Pingora checks. Allocation calls are broadly unchanged; there is no new throughput, P99 or hardware-contention qualification. All accepted and rejected measurements remain in the record; the changes are local pending mainline delivery.

+The [clock, producer-shard and route-position follow-up](validation-hyper-instructions5-2026-10-24.md) measures clock calls, native producer placement, snapshot route positions and repeated header names independently. Header-name cache trials reduced instructions but did not qualify on CPU cost, and were withdrawn. The accepted changes retain precise timing, request and idle-pool budgets, public metric observations and snapshot lifetimes. See the report for final instruction controls, interleaved CPU qualification and rejected-trial evidence.
+
 ## Earlier measurements

 The [round-nine comparison](validation-performance-round9-2026-09-27.md) measured plain HTTP/1, two workers, 64 connections, three alternating 8-second windows after warmup, on shared OrbStack Linux ARM64. Access logging/OTLP output was disabled; product policies and metrics remained active.
